\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {1}{\ignorespaces The edit-and-continue protocol. One written step of a correct worked solution is altered and the model continues from it; the readout is whether the final answer builds on the altered value. The interventions: (1) edit the visible text of the step; (2) overwrite the hidden state at the value's token, leaving the text unchanged; (3) block attention from later positions to the value's token.}}{2}{figure.1}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:protocol}{{1}{2}{The edit-and-continue protocol. One written step of a correct worked solution is altered and the model continues from it; the readout is whether the final answer builds on the altered value. The interventions: (1) edit the visible text of the step; (2) overwrite the hidden state at the value's token, leaving the text unchanged; (3) block attention from later positions to the value's token}{figure.1}{}}
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {section}{\numberline {2}Tasks and protocol}{2}{section.2}\protected@file@percent }
\citation{gurnee2026jspace}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {2}{\ignorespaces Writing is not triggered by exhausted internal capacity. (A)~Instructed to answer without writing, models collapse after one to two dependent steps; with writing allowed, accuracy stays near ceiling ($n{=}30$ items per depth). (B)~The fraction of intermediate values written is 1.00 at every depth (30 to 1,920 values per depth; 95 percent Wilson intervals), so writing begins at no threshold. (C)~No intervention moves state between the workspace and the trace: J-space ablation and random directions leave accuracy unchanged (GSM8K, Qwen3-4B); residual lesions hurt the internally held box-tracking task three times more than the written chain task; a token cap below the per-step floor collapses accuracy by truncation (DeepSeek V3.2, $d{=}16$).}}{3}{figure.2}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:capacity}{{2}{3}{Writing is not triggered by exhausted internal capacity. (A)~Instructed to answer without writing, models collapse after one to two dependent steps; with writing allowed, accuracy stays near ceiling ($n{=}30$ items per depth). (B)~The fraction of intermediate values written is 1.00 at every depth (30 to 1,920 values per depth; 95 percent Wilson intervals), so writing begins at no threshold. (C)~No intervention moves state between the workspace and the trace: J-space ablation and random directions leave accuracy unchanged (GSM8K, Qwen3-4B); residual lesions hurt the internally held box-tracking task three times more than the written chain task; a token cap below the per-step floor collapses accuracy by truncation (DeepSeek V3.2, $d{=}16$)}{figure.2}{}}
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {section}{\numberline {3}The internal workspace holds a few steps at most}{3}{section.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{sec:nohome}{{3}{3}{The internal workspace holds a few steps at most}{section.3}{}}
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {3}{\ignorespaces The hidden state under a written value is a settable register, and two registers compose. (A)~The text still says 457; the hidden state at that token now encodes 462, which appears nowhere, and the final answer continues from 462. (B)~Fraction of runs whose final answer uses the injected value; bars are 95 percent bootstrap intervals over items. The reasoning-distilled models re-solve after their reasoning phase, which raises their random-control rate; re-derivation can only produce the correct answer. (C,~D)~With two counters $A$ and $B$, injecting a replacement for either or both ($a'$, $b'$) makes the answer equal the matching sum; answers using only one of two injected values occur at 0.01.}}{4}{figure.3}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:registers}{{3}{4}{The hidden state under a written value is a settable register, and two registers compose. (A)~The text still says 457; the hidden state at that token now encodes 462, which appears nowhere, and the final answer continues from 462. (B)~Fraction of runs whose final answer uses the injected value; bars are 95 percent bootstrap intervals over items. The reasoning-distilled models re-solve after their reasoning phase, which raises their random-control rate; re-derivation can only produce the correct answer. (C,~D)~With two counters $A$ and $B$, injecting a replacement for either or both ($a'$, $b'$) makes the answer equal the matching sum; answers using only one of two injected values occur at 0.01}{figure.3}{}}
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {section}{\numberline {4}The written position holds a settable value register}{4}{section.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{sec:register}{{4}{4}{The written position holds a settable value register}{section.4}{}}
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {paragraph}{The result is a property of written state, not of one template.}{4}{section*.1}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {4}{\ignorespaces Written values are retrieved through attention to their token, across the middle third of layers. (A)~Blocking later positions' attention to the edited value's token drops edit use to zero on four models; matched control blocks change nothing ($n{=}600$ per condition per model). (B)~Overwriting the hidden state at any single layer up to 22 redirects the answer; from layer 24 on it does nothing (Qwen3-4B, 36 layers, $n{=}60$). (C)~Blocking attention across layers 12 to 23 (shaded in both panels) removes 0.83 of edit use; no single layer's block matters (gray dots, $n{=}80$).}}{5}{figure.4}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:retrieval}{{4}{5}{Written values are retrieved through attention to their token, across the middle third of layers. (A)~Blocking later positions' attention to the edited value's token drops edit use to zero on four models; matched control blocks change nothing ($n{=}600$ per condition per model). (B)~Overwriting the hidden state at any single layer up to 22 redirects the answer; from layer 24 on it does nothing (Qwen3-4B, 36 layers, $n{=}60$). (C)~Blocking attention across layers 12 to 23 (shaded in both panels) removes 0.83 of edit use; no single layer's block matters (gray dots, $n{=}80$)}{figure.4}{}}
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {paragraph}{Written positions are independently addressable.}{5}{section*.2}\protected@file@percent }
\@writefile{toc}{\contentsline {section}{\numberline {5}Retrieval runs through attention to the written position}{5}{section.5}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{sec:read}{{5}{5}{Retrieval runs through attention to the written position}{section.5}{}}
